hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27701","Haddathana Sufyan from Amr from Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim from Abu Shurayh al-Khuzai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him do good to his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or keep silent."
"27702","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said who said: Haddathana Ibn Abi Dhib who said: Haddathana Said, meaning al-Maqburi, who said: I heard Abu Shurayh al-Kabi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, made Makkah sacred, and the people did not make it sacred; so whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not shed blood in it nor cut a tree in it; and if one seeks a concession and says it was made lawful for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then Allah made it lawful for me and did not make it lawful for the people, and it at this hour of mine is sacred until the Hour comes; indeed you, company of Khuzaa, killed this slain one, and I will pay his blood-money; so whoever has one slain after this statement of mine, his family are between two choices: either they kill or they take the blood-money."
"27703","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said who said: Haddathana Malik who said: Haddathani Said ibn Abi Said from Abu Shurayh al-Kabi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or keep silent; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; his prize is a day and a night, and hospitality is three days, and whatever is after that is charity; it is not lawful for him to stay with him until he expels him."
"27704","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun who said: Akhbarana Ibn Abi Dhib from al-Maqburi from Abu Shurayh al-Kabi that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe, by Allah he does not believe; they said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah; he said: The neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his bawaiq; they said: O Messenger of Allah, and what are his bawaiq; he said: His evil."
"27705","Haddathana Safwan who said: Akhbarana Abd Allah ibn Said from his father from Abu Shurayh ibn Amr al-Khuzai who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of sitting on the roads; so whoever of you sits on the road, let him give it its right; he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, and what is its right; he said: Lowering the gaze, returning the greeting, commanding good and forbidding evil."
"27706","Haddathana Abu Kamil who said: Haddathana Layth who said: Haddathani Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi that he said to Amr ibn Said while he was sending troops to Makkah: Permit me, O commander, to tell you a statement with which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood the morrow of the day of the conquest; my two ears heard it and my heart retained it and my two eyes saw him when he spoke it: that he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Indeed Makkah was made sacred by Allah and the people did not make it sacred; so it is not lawful for a person who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood in it nor to cut a tree in it; and if anyone seeks concession by the fighting of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it, then say: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, permitted His Messenger and did not permit you; and it was only permitted for me in it for an hour of the day, and its sanctity has returned today as its sanctity yesterday; so let the witness convey to the absent; so it was said to Abu Shurayh: What did Amr say to you; he said: He said: I know that better than you, O Abu Shurayh; indeed the sanctuary does not grant refuge to a disobedient one, nor to one fleeing with blood, nor to one fleeing with jizya; and likewise Hajjaj said: with jizya; and Yaqub said from his father from Ibn Ishaq: nor to one withholding jizya."
"27707","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Bakr who said: Haddathana Abd al-Hamid who said: Akhbarani Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi from Abu Shurayh al-Adawi of Khuzaa, and he was of the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Hospitality is three, and his prize is a day and a night; and it is not lawful for anyone to stay with his brother until he causes him sin; they said: O Messenger of Allah, what causes him sin; he said: He stays with him and he finds nothing to feed him."
